title 'Check for Understanding'

question 'A developer is choosing between two function names: `markAsRead()` and `update1()`. Both work in code. Why is `markAsRead()` the better choice?'

wrong 'It runs faster than `update1()`.'
wrong 'Function names ending in `Read()` are required by JavaScript.'
right 'It describes what the user experiences, which helps both human developers and AI tools understand and reuse the code correctly.'
wrong '`update1()` would cause a syntax error.'

